{"type":"message","id":"33aca223","parentId":"c16600c6","timestamp":"2026-04-01T16:06:42.677Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bqTiKRBsypSgJgqHBj5aafmK|fc_05a6eafc242db68f0169cd429088f8819199767cae0dd5b475","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues \\\"silently sandboxes all skills\\\"\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1653,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"524888189fb31c90\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Sandbox mode accepts config without validating Docker ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"524888189fb31c90\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/9543\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"33fba56ed84fa23a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nsandbox.mode: \\\"non-main\\\" or \\\"all\\\") without Docker installed causes isolated sessions (cron jobs, spawned sub-agents) to fail silently.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"33fba56ed84fa23a\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99995863\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7bdce488b7891b14\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug] PTY silently disabled in sandbox mode without warning when ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7bdce488b7891b14\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/38601\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0049c14df011dab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Bug] PTY silently disabled in sandbox mode without warning when pty:true is set #38601. [[Bug] PTY silently disabled in sandbox mode without warning when pty:true is set](#top)#38601. When a user sets `pty: true` on the `exec` tool but the session is running in sandbox mode, PTY is silently disabled without any warning to the user. The PTY is forcibly disabled when `sandbox` is true, but no warning is added to the `warnings` array to inform the user. Users following the `coding-agent` skill documentation will have broken experiences in sandbox mode. 2. **Silent behavior change**: Users explicitly set `pty: true` expecting PTY to be enabled, but it's silently ignored in sandbox mode. When `pty: true` is set but sandbox mode is active, the system should:. 1. **Add a warning** to inform the user that PTY is not available in sandbox mode, OR. `docs/refactor/exec-host.md` mentions \\\"PTY supported in non-sandbox mode only\\\" but this is a refactor plan document, not user-facing documentation.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0049c14df011dab\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999502\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58593c2e330601e3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Custom workspace skills with `~/.openclaw/workspace/skills ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58593c2e330601e3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/40154\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab8bbe42c5054ec7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe affected skills are user workspace skills located under: ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/meeting-guide/SKILL.md\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab8bbe42c5054ec7\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9998313\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a4ff4ee116df250\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: OpenClaw treats codex exec sandbox-denied runs ... - GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a4ff4ee116df250\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39317\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5907a0b3f757c723\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n# [Bug]: OpenClaw treats codex exec sandbox-denied runs as success because codex exits 0 #39317. [[Bug]: OpenClaw treats codex exec sandbox-denied runs as success because codex exits 0](#top)#39317. OpenClaw can treat failed `codex exec --json` runs as successful because Codex may emit sandbox/write-denied failure information in JSONL agent output while still exiting with status code `0`. 4. Observe that Codex emits JSONL events describing the write failure as agent output. OpenClaw should inspect Codex JSONL output for failed action/tool signals and propagate the run as failed when the underlying file mutation or command execution was denied or rejected. A Codex run can fail semantically while still looking successful to OpenClaw because:. Affected: Users relying on Codex-backed subagents or Codex fallback runs for coding/file tasks. Frequency: Reproducible whenever Codex surfaces the failure only through JSONL content while exiting 0. A robust fix is to parse Codex JSONL for failed `command_execution` / `shell_command` / `file_change` items and known sandbox-denied agent messages instead of relying only on process exit status.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5907a0b3f757c723\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99981767\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6cbf2101c9e71fc9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nConfigurable behavior for unavailable tool dispatch #17829 - GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6cbf2101c9e71fc9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/17829\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ef97f2a35762eb6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNote: This is specifically about skill command dispatch, not about sandbox policy tool blocking (which has its own separate messaging). In multi\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ef97f2a35762eb6\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99980134\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues \"silently sandboxes all skills\"","provider":"tavily","count":5,"tookMs":1653,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"524888189fb31c90\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Sandbox mode accepts config without validating Docker ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"524888189fb31c90\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/9543","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"33fba56ed84fa23a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nsandbox.mode: \"non-main\" or \"all\") without Docker installed causes isolated sessions (cron jobs, spawned sub-agents) to fail silently.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"33fba56ed84fa23a\">>>","score":0.99995863},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7bdce488b7891b14\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug] PTY silently disabled in sandbox mode without warning when ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7bdce488b7891b14\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/38601","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a0049c14df011dab\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug] PTY silently disabled in sandbox mode without warning when pty:true is set #38601. [[Bug] PTY silently disabled in sandbox mode without warning when pty:true is set](#top)#38601. When a user sets `pty: true` on the `exec` tool but the session is running in sandbox mode, PTY is silently disabled without any warning to the user. The PTY is forcibly disabled when `sandbox` is true, but no warning is added to the `warnings` array to inform the user. Users following the `coding-agent` skill documentation will have broken experiences in sandbox mode. 2. **Silent behavior change**: Users explicitly set `pty: true` expecting PTY to be enabled, but it's silently ignored in sandbox mode. When `pty: true` is set but sandbox mode is active, the system should:. 1. **Add a warning** to inform the user that PTY is not available in sandbox mode, OR. `docs/refactor/exec-host.md` mentions \"PTY supported in non-sandbox mode only\" but this is a refactor plan document, not user-facing documentation.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a0049c14df011dab\">>>","score":0.9999502},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58593c2e330601e3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Custom workspace skills with `~/.openclaw/workspace/skills ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58593c2e330601e3\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/40154","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ab8bbe42c5054ec7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe affected skills are user workspace skills located under: ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/meeting-guide/SKILL.md\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ab8bbe42c5054ec7\">>>","score":0.9998313},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4a4ff4ee116df250\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: OpenClaw treats codex exec sandbox-denied runs ... - GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4a4ff4ee116df250\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39317","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5907a0b3f757c723\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: OpenClaw treats codex exec sandbox-denied runs as success because codex exits 0 #39317. [[Bug]: OpenClaw treats codex exec sandbox-denied runs as success because codex exits 0](#top)#39317. OpenClaw can treat failed `codex exec --json` runs as successful because Codex may emit sandbox/write-denied failure information in JSONL agent output while still exiting with status code `0`. 4. Observe that Codex emits JSONL events describing the write failure as agent output. OpenClaw should inspect Codex JSONL output for failed action/tool signals and propagate the run as failed when the underlying file mutation or command execution was denied or rejected. A Codex run can fail semantically while still looking successful to OpenClaw because:. Affected: Users relying on Codex-backed subagents