{"type":"message","id":"cca5daaf","parentId":"63b5b177","timestamp":"2026-04-01T16:07:08.939Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_tjTn4DeUeL8xdHgyZrlo8j1U|fc_05a6eafc242db68f0169cd42aad1788191b880a280d5a17561","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues Weixin plugin openclaw updated 2026.3.31\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1745,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2d918145a97a7e1e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIndependent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat · Issue #52537 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2d918145a97a7e1e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52537\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"748d6ce9fcc59af1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat · Issue #52537 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat #52537. Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat#52537. ## Description. opened on Mar 23, 2026. ## Problem. Two related issues when using independent agents with the WeChat (openclaw-weixin) channel:. Independent agent does not inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault`. When `thinkingDefault: \\\"off\\\"` is set under `agents.defaults`, independent agents (created via `openclaw agents add`) do **not** inherit this setting. New sessions created by inbound messages from the WeChat channel are missing the `reasoning:off` / `think:off` flag. * Main agent session: `reasoning:off` ✅. * Independent wechat agent session: no flag ❌. Attempting to add `thinkingDefault` to `agents.list[].` config is rejected with `Unrecognized key: \\\"thinkingDefault\\\"`. openclaw-weixin plugin does not filter thinking/reasoning output. The WeChat plugin (`openclaw-weixin`) transparently forwards the full model response to the WeChat chat, including reasoning/thinking blocks. The Telegram channel correctly strips these before sending to the user. Grep of the weixin plugin source (`src/`) shows zero references to `thinking` or `reasoning` — no filtering logic exists. ### Expected behavior. 1. Independent agents should inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault` (or support per-agent `thinkingDefault` config). 2. The WeChat plugin should strip thinking/reasoning content from outbound messages, consistent with Telegram behavior. ### Environment. * OpenClaw 2026.3.13 (61d171a). * openclaw-weixin@1.0.2. ### Workaround. Setting `reasoning: false` in the agent's `models.json` is unreliable as it gets overwritten by config sync. No effective workaround currently exists. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"748d6ce9fcc59af1\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.8055255\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"622d9f97af5f061a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run · Issue #46955 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"622d9f97af5f061a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/46955\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71505d4496cf6ad6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: Bug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run · Issue #46955 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Bug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run #46955. Bug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run#46955. ## Description. opened on Mar 15, 2026. ## Bug Description. `openclaw update --yes` re-downloads, extracts, and reinstalls the npm plugin `@martian-engineering/lossless-claw` on every run, even when the installed plugin version is unchanged. The updater output ends with:. * `npm plugins: 0 updated, 1 unchanged.`. * rewrites `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` (`changedPaths=2`). ## Reproduction. 1. Install `@martian-engineering/lossless-claw` via `openclaw plugins install`. 2. Ensure the plugin is already at the current npm version. 3. Run `openclaw update --yes`. 4. Run `openclaw update --yes` again without any plugin version change. ## Actual Behavior. Each update run re-downloads and reinstalls the plugin and overwrites config, even though the plugin is reported as unchanged. Downloading @martian-engineering/lossless-claw… Extracting .../martian-engineering-lossless-claw-0.3.0.tgz… Plugin \\\"lossless-claw\\\" has 1 suspicious code pattern(s). Run \\\"openclaw security audit --deep\\\" for details. Installing to /home/agent_smith/.openclaw/extensions/lossless-claw… Installing plugin dependencies… Config overwrite: ... changedPaths=2 npm plugins: 0 updated, 1 unchanged. ## Expected Behavior. If the resolved plugin version/integrity is unchanged, `openclaw update` should skip extract/install/dependency-install and avoid rewriting `openclaw.json`. If this behavior is intentional (for integrity verification or repair), the CLI should report that explicitly instead of reporting the plugin as unchanged. ## Impact. * Adds ~30 seconds to every `openclaw update`. * Causes daily config churn when updates are automated (via timer). * Increases risk of config write races / lost updates with concurrent changes. ## Environment. * OpenClaw version: 2026.3.13 (61d171a). * Plugin: `@martian-engineering/lossless-claw` `0.3.0`. * OS: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (headless server). ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71505d4496cf6ad6\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.80014634\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4dc1d8dd6f54e360\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages · Issue #52086 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4dc1d8dd6f54e360\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52086\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a22dd59c99c896cf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages · Issue #52086 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages #52086. [[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages](#top)#52086. ## Description. opened on Mar 22, 2026. ## Feature Request. ### Problem. When a user forwards a WeChat Official Account (公众号) article to the bot, the message is silently dropped — the agent receives nothing. This makes it impossible to discuss or process shared articles. ### Expected Behavior. When a link/article message is forwarded, the agent should receive at minimum:. * **URL** (the `mp.weixin.qq.com` link). * **Description/summary** (if available from the message payload). ### Additional Context. * WeChat link messages have type `49` (app message) with sub-types for articles. * The XML payload contains , ,  fields that can be extracted. * Even just passing the title + URL as a text message would be a huge improvement. * Server-side fetching of article content is blocked by WeChat anti-scraping (CAPTCHA), so extracting content on the client side before forwarding would be ideal as a follow-up enhancement. ### Environment. * Plugin: `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.2. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a22dd59c99c896cf\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.78963995\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9dc1de478e2da21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used · Issue #52153 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9dc1de478e2da21\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52153\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"731168fa9b59cce5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: WeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used · Issue #52153 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # WeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used #52153. WeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used#52153. ## Description. opened on Mar 22, 2026. **Scenario**: After gateway restart, automatically send WeChat message to notify user \\\"ready\\\" via BOOT.md. 1. boot-md triggers message tool to send WeChat message and fails. 2. Error: sendWeixinOutbound: contextToken is required. 3. Reason: WeChat sending requires contextToken (session context token), but boot-md is headless startup without active session, cannot obtain contextToken. 4. QQ plugin supports proactive sending via dmPolicy configuration, but WeChat plugin lacks similar configuration. 1. WeChat plugin supports dmPolicy configuration like QQ to allow proactive message sending. 2. Or automatically obtain/create session when no contextToken. 3. Or provide another way to send WeChat messages in BOOT.md. * WeChat plugin: @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin v1.0.2. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"731168fa9b59cce5\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.7730283\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5e5bd93451ecb45e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5e5bd93451ecb45e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15d1775d806129df\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. ## Description. opened on Mar 23, 2026. ## 问题描述. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. ## 错误信息. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\.openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\openclaw-weixin\\\\index.ts. ## 根本原因. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{withFileLock} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. export{buildFalImageGenerationProvider, buildGoogleImageGenerationProvider, buildOpenAIImageGenerationProvider, delegateCompactionToRuntime, emptyPluginConfigSchema, onDiagnosticEvent, registerContextEngine};. ## 环境信息. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. ## 建议修复. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. ## 临时解决尝试. 2. 为插件创建 node\\\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\\\_PATH 环境变量. ## 相关链接. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15d1775d806129df\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.7557276\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e47b1c3f40dd053a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nv2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e47b1c3f40dd053a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/54790\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5008d7ebfb3651c9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 #54790. v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13#54790. * Install method: `npm install -g openclaw`. * Service management: launchd (`ai.openclaw.gateway`). Upgrading from v2026.3.13 to v2026.3.24 via `openclaw update` caused Gateway crash with multiple packaging/build issues preventing clean restart. ## Issue 1: Gateway crashes during upgrade, launchd fails to auto-restart. **Symptom:** After upgrade, Gateway process terminates. **Root cause:** `npm install -g` overwrites `dist/` in-place while the Gateway is running. [ws] ⇄ res ✗ channels.status 2149ms errorCode=UNAVAILABLE errorMessage=Error: Cannot find module '.../dist/audit-membership-runtime-BT91Am6G.js' imported from '.../dist/reply-Bm8VrLQh.js'. **Workaround:** `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/ai.openclaw.gateway`. **Suggestion:** `openclaw update` should gracefully stop the Gateway before replacing dist files, then restart. ## Issue 2: memory-lancedb plugin fails — `dist/package.json` missing from npm package. [plugins] memory-lancedb failed to load: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.../openclaw/dist/package.json'. **Root cause:** `dist/lancedb-runtime-3m75WU-W.js` line 10 reads `package.json` relative to `import.meta.url` (resolves to `dist/`), but the npm package does not include `dist/package.json`. **Workaround:** Manually create `dist/package.json` with `{\\\"dependencies\\\":{\\\"@lancedb/lancedb\\\":\\\"^0.27.1\\\"}}` and re-run `npm install` in `dist/extensions/memory-lancedb/`. **Suggestion:** Include `package.json` (or a minimal version) in `dist/` during build, or fix the path resolution to use the root `package.json`. ## Issue 3: ~40 plugin id mismatch warnings. plugins.entries.anthropic: plugin anthropic: plugin id mismatch (manifest uses \\\"anthropic\\\", entry hints \\\"anthropic-provider\\\"). ## Issue 4: AGENTS.md template missing from npm package. [boot] agent run failed: Missing workspace template: AGENTS.md (.../openclaw/dist/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md). Ensure docs/reference/templates are packaged. **Root cause:** Another build/packaging omission — `dist/docs/reference/templates/` not included in the published npm package. ## Issue 5: openclaw-weixin plugin load failure. openclaw-weixin failed during register: Error: Unable to resolve plugin runtime module. All issues stem from **build/packaging gaps** in v2026.3.24:. 1. Missing `dist/package.json` → lancedb runtime break. 2. Missing `dist/docs/reference/templates/` → boot hook break. 3. In-place dist overwrite during live Gateway → module hash mismatch crash. 4. Plugin id rename without entry hint sync → log noise. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5008d7ebfb3651c9\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.7555112\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7685fcd785e9ba0c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7685fcd785e9ba0c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885?timeline_page=1\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6024bf1d9355c72e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. ## Description. opened on Mar 23, 2026. ## 问题描述. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. ## 错误信息. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\.openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\openclaw-weixin\\\\index.ts. ## 根本原因. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{withFileLock} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\\\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\\\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. export{buildFalImageGenerationProvider, buildGoogleImageGenerationProvider, buildOpenAIImageGenerationProvider, delegateCompactionToRuntime, emptyPluginConfigSchema, onDiagnosticEvent, registerContextEngine};. ## 环境信息. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. ## 建议修复. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. ## 临时解决尝试. 2. 为插件创建 node\\\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\\\_PATH 环境变量. ## 相关链接. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6024bf1d9355c72e\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.74807674\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"76141471244e0b64\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin · Issue #53246 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"76141471244e0b64\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53246\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3d20b36ee7b6b7f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin · Issue #53246 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin #53246. [[Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin](#top)#53246. Enable official Mattermost channel support in OpenClaw by introducing the `@openclaw/mattermost` plugin with gateway-based lifecycle, `defaultTo` configuration, and comprehensive documentation. OpenClaw currently supports several messaging channels (e.g., Slack, Discord, Teams), but lacks native Mattermost integration. Users operating self-hosted Mattermost instances — common in enterprise and open-source environments — cannot use OpenClaw for automated notifications, cron-based alerts, or AI-driven message delivery. Introduce the `@openclaw/mattermost` extension as an officially supported channel plugin with the following capabilities:. * **`defaultTo` support**: Allows outbound message delivery to a pre-configured target channel when no explicit target is specified (e.g., scheduled cron jobs or system alerts). * **Secure credential management**: All sensitive values (bot tokens, server URLs) are handled exclusively through OpenClaw's secrets framework — no hardcoded credentials anywhere in code or documentation. * **Placeholder-safe documentation**: `docs/mattermost.md` and `README.md` use obvious placeholders (`mm-token-1234`, `https://chat.example.com`) throughout all examples. * **Full test coverage**: 289 unit tests across 34 files covering monitoring, gating, and target resolution — all passing under `pnpm test -- extensions/mattermost/`. **Reference branch**: `feature-mattermost-channel` (branched from `main`, ported from validated `ws_mm_pn_20260322_1930` workspace). **Reference PR**: main...feature-mattermost-channel. | Generic HTTP channel with manual Mattermost calls | No structured lifecycle, no `defaultTo`, no test coverage; brittle and unsupported |. The plugin architecture with gateway integration is the only approach that delivers a consistent, secure, and maintainable first-class channel experience aligned with OpenClaw's existing design. * **Affected users/systems**: All OpenClaw users operating self-hosted or cloud Mattermost instances; particularly enterprise teams using Mattermost as their primary internal communications platform. * **Severity**: Blocks workflow — there is currently no supported, standards-compliant path to connect OpenClaw with Mattermost. * **Frequency**: Affects every interaction where Mattermost is the intended delivery channel (always reproducible — the channel simply does not exist). * 289/289 unit tests pass: `pnpm test -- extensions/mattermost/`. * `README.md` updated to list Mattermost alongside existing supported channels. * This issue tracks the review and merge of PR `feat(mattermost): enable Mattermost channel support via plugin`.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3d20b36ee7b6b7f\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.6922474\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7963e563ba31a8a2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 · Issue #52341 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7963e563ba31a8a2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52341\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a66d63eb067d985f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 · Issue #52341 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... There was an error while loading. # [Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 #52341. [[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14](#top)#52341. After installing `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@1.0.2` into a local OpenClaw `2026.3.14` source checkout on macOS 26.2, the Weixin plugin does not load consistently: gateway startup logs `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'` or `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/core'`, and CLI plugin loading logs `TypeError: (0 , _pluginSdk.resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir) is not a function`. In this state the Weixin account never stays active, so inbound Weixin messages are not processed. 1. Use an OpenClaw `2026.3.14` source checkout on macOS 26.2 (`pnpm install`, `pnpm build`). 2. Install `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@1.0.2`. 4. Run `pnpm openclaw channels status --probe --json` and inspect the gateway log. 5. Observe plugin load failures instead of a stable running Weixin channel. After installation and QR login, the external Weixin plugin should load under both gateway startup and CLI/plugin-registry loading, and `channels status` should show a running Weixin account without plugin load errors. The plugin loader fails during startup/registry load. * `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. * `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/core'`. When this happens, the gateway comes up with Telegram only, or the Weixin channel appears only after local compatibility hacks. Without those hacks, Weixin inbound messages are not handled. ### OpenClaw version. Source checkout (`pnpm install`, `pnpm build`, then `pnpm openclaw ...`). openai-codex/gpt-5.4. ### Additional provider/model setup details. No special provider routing was needed to reproduce the plugin load failure. ;'openclaw/plugin-sdk' ' ''openclaw/plugin-sdk' ' '. Related existing issue: #52153 is about proactive sending on Weixin; this report is about plugin loading / SDK compatibility before normal runtime behavior. Affected: local/source OpenClaw installs using the external `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` plugin. Frequency: Reproduced repeatedly across gateway restarts and `channels status --probe --json` runs. Consequence: The Weixin plugin does not load reliably, so the channel cannot be used normally. I also observed a separate Weixin symptom where replies could arrive in the wrong order after local compatibility hacks, but I do not yet have a clean minimal repro or log set for that behavior. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a66d63eb067d985f\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.69024646\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca6ed91148281cbf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/ · Issue #53273 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca6ed91148281cbf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53273\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"62704912d82649c6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/ · Issue #53273 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/ #53273. [[Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/](#top)#53273. After upgrading OpenClaw via `npm install -g openclaw`, the gateway fails to start with a config validation error because the `acpx` plugin path in `openclaw.json` is not automatically migrated from the old layout (`extensions/acpx`) to the new one (`dist/extensions/acpx`). * **OS:** Windows 10 (10.0.26100 x64). * **OpenClaw version (after upgrade):** 2026.3.23-1. * **Install method:** `npm install -g openclaw` (standard npm global install). 1. Have an existing OpenClaw installation with `acpx` plugin configured. 2. Run `npm install -g openclaw` to upgrade. ## Actual Behavior. Gateway fails with config validation error on every startup:. Config invalid - plugins.load.paths: plugin: plugin path not found: D:\\\\Program Files\\\\nodejs\\\\npm-global\\\\node_modules\\\\openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\acpx Run: openclaw doctor --fix. Inspecting the package, the actual path after upgrade is:. D:\\\\Program Files\\\\nodejs\\\\npm-global\\\\node_modules\\\\openclaw\\\\dist\\\\extensions\\\\acpx. The `openclaw.json` config still contains the old path in two fields:. \\\"plugins\\\" \\\"installs\\\" \\\"acpx\\\" \\\"sourcePath\\\"\\\"...\\\\\\\\openclaw\\\\\\\\extensions\\\\\\\\acpx\\\" \\\" \\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\ \\\" \\\"installPath\\\"\\\"...\\\\\\\\openclaw\\\\\\\\extensions\\\\\\\\acpx\\\" \\\" \\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\ \\\". ## Expected Behavior. * The upgrade process (or first run after upgrade) automatically migrates `plugins.installs.acpx.sourcePath` and `plugins.installs.acpx.installPath` to the new `dist/extensions/acpx` path, **or**. * `openclaw doctor --fix` detects and fixes this stale path automatically. * `openclaw doctor --fix` was run but did **not** fix the path issue (it reported `Plugins: Loaded: 4, Errors: 0`, which appears incorrect given the gateway was logging errors). * The Control UI showed a red \\\"Update available\\\" banner after the upgrade even though the installed version was already the latest — this may be a related symptom. * Manual fix: edit `openclaw.json` and update both `sourcePath` and `installPath` to point to `dist/extensions/acpx`. Manually update `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`:. \\\"plugins\\\" \\\"installs\\\" \\\"acpx\\\" \\\"sourcePath\\\"\\\"/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/acpx\\\" \\\" \\\" \\\"installPath\\\"\\\"/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/acpx\\\" \\\" \\\". ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"62704912d82649c6\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.6892434\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues Weixin plugin openclaw updated 2026.3.31","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":1745,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2d918145a97a7e1e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIndependent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat · Issue #52537 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2d918145a97a7e1e\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52537","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"748d6ce9fcc59af1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat · Issue #52537 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat #52537. Independent agent does not inherit thinkingDefault; WeChat plugin leaks reasoning to chat#52537. ## Description. opened on Mar 23, 2026. ## Problem. Two related issues when using independent agents with the WeChat (openclaw-weixin) channel:. Independent agent does not inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault`. When `thinkingDefault: \"off\"` is set under `agents.defaults`, independent agents (created via `openclaw agents add`) do **not** inherit this setting. New sessions created by inbound messages from the WeChat channel are missing the `reasoning:off` / `think:off` flag. * Main agent session: `reasoning:off` ✅. * Independent wechat agent session: no flag ❌. Attempting to add `thinkingDefault` to `agents.list[].` config is rejected with `Unrecognized key: \"thinkingDefault\"`. openclaw-weixin plugin does not filter thinking/reasoning output. The WeChat plugin (`openclaw-weixin`) transparently forwards the full model response to the WeChat chat, including reasoning/thinking blocks. The Telegram channel correctly strips these before sending to the user. Grep of the weixin plugin source (`src/`) shows zero references to `thinking` or `reasoning` — no filtering logic exists. ### Expected behavior. 1. Independent agents should inherit `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault` (or support per-agent `thinkingDefault` config). 2. The WeChat plugin should strip thinking/reasoning content from outbound messages, consistent with Telegram behavior. ### Environment. * OpenClaw 2026.3.13 (61d171a). * openclaw-weixin@1.0.2. ### Workaround. Setting `reasoning: false` in the agent's `models.json` is unreliable as it gets overwritten by config sync. No effective workaround currently exists. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"748d6ce9fcc59af1\">>>","score":0.8055255},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"622d9f97af5f061a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nBug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run · Issue #46955 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"622d9f97af5f061a\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/46955","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71505d4496cf6ad6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: Bug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run · Issue #46955 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Bug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run #46955. Bug: openclaw update reinstalls unchanged npm plugins and rewrites openclaw.json on every run#46955. ## Description. opened on Mar 15, 2026. ## Bug Description. `openclaw update --yes` re-downloads, extracts, and reinstalls the npm plugin `@martian-engineering/lossless-claw` on every run, even when the installed plugin version is unchanged. The updater output ends with:. * `npm plugins: 0 updated, 1 unchanged.`. * rewrites `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` (`changedPaths=2`). ## Reproduction. 1. Install `@martian-engineering/lossless-claw` via `openclaw plugins install`. 2. Ensure the plugin is already at the current npm version. 3. Run `openclaw update --yes`. 4. Run `openclaw update --yes` again without any plugin version change. ## Actual Behavior. Each update run re-downloads and reinstalls the plugin and overwrites config, even though the plugin is reported as unchanged. Downloading @martian-engineering/lossless-claw… Extracting .../martian-engineering-lossless-claw-0.3.0.tgz… Plugin \"lossless-claw\" has 1 suspicious code pattern(s). Run \"openclaw security audit --deep\" for details. Installing to /home/agent_smith/.openclaw/extensions/lossless-claw… Installing plugin dependencies… Config overwrite: ... changedPaths=2 npm plugins: 0 updated, 1 unchanged. ## Expected Behavior. If the resolved plugin version/integrity is unchanged, `openclaw update` should skip extract/install/dependency-install and avoid rewriting `openclaw.json`. If this behavior is intentional (for integrity verification or repair), the CLI should report that explicitly instead of reporting the plugin as unchanged. ## Impact. * Adds ~30 seconds to every `openclaw update`. * Causes daily config churn when updates are automated (via timer). * Increases risk of config write races / lost updates with concurrent changes. ## Environment. * OpenClaw version: 2026.3.13 (61d171a). * Plugin: `@martian-engineering/lossless-claw` `0.3.0`. * OS: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (headless server). ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71505d4496cf6ad6\">>>","score":0.80014634},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4dc1d8dd6f54e360\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages · Issue #52086 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4dc1d8dd6f54e360\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52086","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a22dd59c99c896cf\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages · Issue #52086 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages #52086. [[openclaw-weixin] Support receiving forwarded WeChat article (link) messages](#top)#52086. ## Description. opened on Mar 22, 2026. ## Feature Request. ### Problem. When a user forwards a WeChat Official Account (公众号) article to the bot, the message is silently dropped — the agent receives nothing. This makes it impossible to discuss or process shared articles. ### Expected Behavior. When a link/article message is forwarded, the agent should receive at minimum:. * **URL** (the `mp.weixin.qq.com` link). * **Description/summary** (if available from the message payload). ### Additional Context. * WeChat link messages have type `49` (app message) with sub-types for articles. * The XML payload contains , ,  fields that can be extracted. * Even just passing the title + URL as a text message would be a huge improvement. * Server-side fetching of article content is blocked by WeChat anti-scraping (CAPTCHA), so extracting content on the client side before forwarding would be ideal as a follow-up enhancement. ### Environment. * Plugin: `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.2. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a22dd59c99c896cf\">>>","score":0.78963995},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a9dc1de478e2da21\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used · Issue #52153 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a9dc1de478e2da21\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52153","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"731168fa9b59cce5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: WeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used · Issue #52153 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # WeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used #52153. WeChat plugin does not support proactive sending messages, BOOT.md scenario cannot be used#52153. ## Description. opened on Mar 22, 2026. **Scenario**: After gateway restart, automatically send WeChat message to notify user \"ready\" via BOOT.md. 1. boot-md triggers message tool to send WeChat message and fails. 2. Error: sendWeixinOutbound: contextToken is required. 3. Reason: WeChat sending requires contextToken (session context token), but boot-md is headless startup without active session, cannot obtain contextToken. 4. QQ plugin supports proactive sending via dmPolicy configuration, but WeChat plugin lacks similar configuration. 1. WeChat plugin supports dmPolicy configuration like QQ to allow proactive message sending. 2. Or automatically obtain/create session when no contextToken. 3. Or provide another way to send WeChat messages in BOOT.md. * WeChat plugin: @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin v1.0.2. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"731168fa9b59cce5\">>>","score":0.7730283},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5e5bd93451ecb45e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5e5bd93451ecb45e\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"15d1775d806129df\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. ## Description. opened on Mar 23, 2026. ## 问题描述. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. ## 错误信息. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\extensions\\openclaw-weixin\\index.ts. ## 根本原因. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{withFileLock} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. export{buildFalImageGenerationProvider, buildGoogleImageGenerationProvider, buildOpenAIImageGenerationProvider, delegateCompactionToRuntime, emptyPluginConfigSchema, onDiagnosticEvent, registerContextEngine};. ## 环境信息. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. ## 建议修复. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. ## 临时解决尝试. 2. 为插件创建 node\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\_PATH 环境变量. ## 相关链接. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"15d1775d806129df\">>>","score":0.7557276},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e47b1c3f40dd053a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nv2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e47b1c3f40dd053a\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/54790","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5008d7ebfb3651c9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 · Issue #54790 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13 #54790. v2026.3.24: Multiple packaging/build issues cause Gateway crash on upgrade from v2026.3.13#54790. * Install method: `npm install -g openclaw`. * Service management: launchd (`ai.openclaw.gateway`). Upgrading from v2026.3.13 to v2026.3.24 via `openclaw update` caused Gateway crash with multiple packaging/build issues preventing clean restart. ## Issue 1: Gateway crashes during upgrade, launchd fails to auto-restart. **Symptom:** After upgrade, Gateway process terminates. **Root cause:** `npm install -g` overwrites `dist/` in-place while the Gateway is running. [ws] ⇄ res ✗ channels.status 2149ms errorCode=UNAVAILABLE errorMessage=Error: Cannot find module '.../dist/audit-membership-runtime-BT91Am6G.js' imported from '.../dist/reply-Bm8VrLQh.js'. **Workaround:** `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/ai.openclaw.gateway`. **Suggestion:** `openclaw update` should gracefully stop the Gateway before replacing dist files, then restart. ## Issue 2: memory-lancedb plugin fails — `dist/package.json` missing from npm package. [plugins] memory-lancedb failed to load: Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.../openclaw/dist/package.json'. **Root cause:** `dist/lancedb-runtime-3m75WU-W.js` line 10 reads `package.json` relative to `import.meta.url` (resolves to `dist/`), but the npm package does not include `dist/package.json`. **Workaround:** Manually create `dist/package.json` with `{\"dependencies\":{\"@lancedb/lancedb\":\"^0.27.1\"}}` and re-run `npm install` in `dist/extensions/memory-lancedb/`. **Suggestion:** Include `package.json` (or a minimal version) in `dist/` during build, or fix the path resolution to use the root `package.json`. ## Issue 3: ~40 plugin id mismatch warnings. plugins.entries.anthropic: plugin anthropic: plugin id mismatch (manifest uses \"anthropic\", entry hints \"anthropic-provider\"). ## Issue 4: AGENTS.md template missing from npm package. [boot] agent run failed: Missing workspace template: AGENTS.md (.../openclaw/dist/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md). Ensure docs/reference/templates are packaged. **Root cause:** Another build/packaging omission — `dist/docs/reference/templates/` not included in the published npm package. ## Issue 5: openclaw-weixin plugin load failure. openclaw-weixin failed during register: Error: Unable to resolve plugin runtime module. All issues stem from **build/packaging gaps** in v2026.3.24:. 1. Missing `dist/package.json` → lancedb runtime break. 2. Missing `dist/docs/reference/templates/` → boot hook break. 3. In-place dist overwrite during live Gateway → module hash mismatch crash. 4. Plugin id rename without entry hint sync → log noise. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5008d7ebfb3651c9\">>>","score":0.7555112},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7685fcd785e9ba0c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7685fcd785e9ba0c\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52885?timeline_page=1","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6024bf1d9355c72e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 · Issue #52885 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容 #52885. 微信插件 @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22+ 不兼容#52885. ## Description. opened on Mar 23, 2026. ## 问题描述. 微信插件 `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` v1.0.3 与 OpenClaw 2026.3.22 及更高版本存在兼容性问题。. ## 错误信息. Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk' Require stack: - C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\extensions\\openclaw-weixin\\index.ts. ## 根本原因. 1. 微信插件源码 (`index.ts`) 使用 ESM import 从 `openclaw/plugin-sdk` 导入 API：. import{normalizeAccountId} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{stripMarkdown} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{withFileLock} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{createTypingCallbacks} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\"; import{buildChannelConfigSchema} from\"openclaw/plugin-sdk\";// ... 2. 但 OpenClaw 的 `dist/plugin-sdk/index.js` 没有导出这些函数（它们只在子模块如 `account-id.js`, `bluebubbles.js`, `file-lock.js` 等中可用）. 3. OpenClaw 最新版本 2026.3.23 的 plugin-sdk 导出的函数：. export{buildFalImageGenerationProvider, buildGoogleImageGenerationProvider, buildOpenAIImageGenerationProvider, delegateCompactionToRuntime, emptyPluginConfigSchema, onDiagnosticEvent, registerContextEngine};. ## 环境信息. * OpenClaw 版本：2026.3.22 / 2026.3.23. * Node.js 版本：24.14.0. ## 建议修复. 请在 OpenClaw 的 `src/plugin-sdk/index.ts` 中添加缺失的导出，或发布一个包含编译后 JS 文件的微信插件版本，使插件可以在不依赖源码解析的情况下工作。. ## 临时解决尝试. 2. 为插件创建 node\\_modules 链接. 3. 使用 NODE\\_PATH 环境变量. ## 相关链接. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6024bf1d9355c72e\">>>","score":0.74807674},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"76141471244e0b64\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin · Issue #53246 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"76141471244e0b64\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53246","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3d20b36ee7b6b7f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin · Issue #53246 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\nYou signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. # [Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin #53246. [[Feature]: Add official Mattermost channel support via plugin](#top)#53246. Enable official Mattermost channel support in OpenClaw by introducing the `@openclaw/mattermost` plugin with gateway-based lifecycle, `defaultTo` configuration, and comprehensive documentation. OpenClaw currently supports several messaging channels (e.g., Slack, Discord, Teams), but lacks native Mattermost integration. Users operating self-hosted Mattermost instances — common in enterprise and open-source environments — cannot use OpenClaw for automated notifications, cron-based alerts, or AI-driven message delivery. Introduce the `@openclaw/mattermost` extension as an officially supported channel plugin with the following capabilities:. * **`defaultTo` support**: Allows outbound message delivery to a pre-configured target channel when no explicit target is specified (e.g., scheduled cron jobs or system alerts). * **Secure credential management**: All sensitive values (bot tokens, server URLs) are handled exclusively through OpenClaw's secrets framework — no hardcoded credentials anywhere in code or documentation. * **Placeholder-safe documentation**: `docs/mattermost.md` and `README.md` use obvious placeholders (`mm-token-1234`, `https://chat.example.com`) throughout all examples. * **Full test coverage**: 289 unit tests across 34 files covering monitoring, gating, and target resolution — all passing under `pnpm test -- extensions/mattermost/`. **Reference branch**: `feature-mattermost-channel` (branched from `main`, ported from validated `ws_mm_pn_20260322_1930` workspace). **Reference PR**: main...feature-mattermost-channel. | Generic HTTP channel with manual Mattermost calls | No structured lifecycle, no `defaultTo`, no test coverage; brittle and unsupported |. The plugin architecture with gateway integration is the only approach that delivers a consistent, secure, and maintainable first-class channel experience aligned with OpenClaw's existing design. * **Affected users/systems**: All OpenClaw users operating self-hosted or cloud Mattermost instances; particularly enterprise teams using Mattermost as their primary internal communications platform. * **Severity**: Blocks workflow — there is currently no supported, standards-compliant path to connect OpenClaw with Mattermost. * **Frequency**: Affects every interaction where Mattermost is the intended delivery channel (always reproducible — the channel simply does not exist). * 289/289 unit tests pass: `pnpm test -- extensions/mattermost/`. * `README.md` updated to list Mattermost alongside existing supported channels. * This issue tracks the review and merge of PR `feat(mattermost): enable Mattermost channel support via plugin`.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3d20b36ee7b6b7f\">>>","score":0.6922474},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7963e563ba31a8a2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 · Issue #52341 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7963e563ba31a8a2\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/52341","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a66d63eb067d985f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 · Issue #52341 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... There was an error while loading. # [Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14 #52341. [[Bug]: External openclaw-weixin plugin fails to load on 2026.3.14](#top)#52341. After installing `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@1.0.2` into a local OpenClaw `2026.3.14` source checkout on macOS 26.2, the Weixin plugin does not load consistently: gateway startup logs `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'` or `Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/core'`, and CLI plugin loading logs `TypeError: (0 , _pluginSdk.resolvePreferredOpenClawTmpDir) is not a function`. In this state the Weixin account never stays active, so inbound Weixin messages are not processed. 1. Use an OpenClaw `2026.3.14` source checkout on macOS 26.2 (`pnpm install`, `pnpm build`). 2. Install `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@1.0.2`. 4. Run `pnpm openclaw channels status --probe --json` and inspect the gateway log. 5. Observe plugin load failures instead of a stable running Weixin channel. After installation and QR login, the external Weixin plugin should load under both gateway startup and CLI/plugin-registry loading, and `channels status` should show a running Weixin account without plugin load errors. The plugin loader fails during startup/registry load. * `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. * `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk/core'`. When this happens, the gateway comes up with Telegram only, or the Weixin channel appears only after local compatibility hacks. Without those hacks, Weixin inbound messages are not handled. ### OpenClaw version. Source checkout (`pnpm install`, `pnpm build`, then `pnpm openclaw ...`). openai-codex/gpt-5.4. ### Additional provider/model setup details. No special provider routing was needed to reproduce the plugin load failure. ;'openclaw/plugin-sdk' ' ''openclaw/plugin-sdk' ' '. Related existing issue: #52153 is about proactive sending on Weixin; this report is about plugin loading / SDK compatibility before normal runtime behavior. Affected: local/source OpenClaw installs using the external `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` plugin. Frequency: Reproduced repeatedly across gateway restarts and `channels status --probe --json` runs. Consequence: The Weixin plugin does not load reliably, so the channel cannot be used normally. I also observed a separate Weixin symptom where replies could arrive in the wrong order after local compatibility hacks, but I do not yet have a clean minimal repro or log set for that behavior. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a66d63eb067d985f\">>>","score":0.69024646},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca6ed91148281cbf\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/ · Issue #53273 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca6ed91148281cbf\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53273","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"62704912d82649c6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/ · Issue #53273 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/ #53273. [[Bug] npm install -g upgrade breaks acpx plugin: sourcePath not updated from extensions/ to dist/extensions/](#top)#53273. After upgrading OpenClaw via `npm install -g openclaw`, the gateway fails to start with a config validation error because the `acpx` plugin path in `openclaw.json` is not automatically migrated from the old layout (`extensions/acpx`) to the new one (`dist/extensions/acpx`). * **OS:** Windows 10 (10.0.26100 x64). * **OpenClaw version (after upgrade):** 2026.3.23-1. * **Install method:** `npm install -g openclaw` (standard npm global install). 1. Have an existing OpenClaw installation with `acpx` plugin configured. 2. Run `npm install -g openclaw` to upgrade. ## Actual Behavior. Gateway fails with config validation error on every startup:. Config invalid - plugins.load.paths: plugin: plugin path not found: D:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\npm-global\\node_modules\\openclaw\\extensions\\acpx Run: openclaw doctor --fix. Inspecting the package, the actual path after upgrade is:. D:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\npm-global\\node_modules\\openclaw\\dist\\extensions\\acpx. The `openclaw.json` config still contains the old path in two fields:. \"plugins\" \"installs\" \"acpx\" \"sourcePath\"\"...\\\\openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\acpx\" \" \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \" \"installPath\"\"...\\\\openclaw\\\\extensions\\\\acpx\" \" \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \". ## Expected Behavior. * The upgrade process (or first run after upgrade) automatically migrates `plugins.installs.acpx.sourcePath` and `plugins.installs.acpx.installPath` to the new `dist/extensions/acpx` path, **or**. * `openclaw doctor --fix` detects and fixes this stale path automatically. * `openclaw doctor --fix` was run but did **not** fix the path issue (it reported `Plugins: Loaded: 4, Errors: 0`, which appears incorrect given the gateway was logging errors). * The Control UI showed a red \"Update available\" banner after the upgrade even though the installed version was already the latest — this may be a related symptom. * Manual fix: edit `openclaw.json` and update both `sourcePath` and `installPath` to point to `dist/extensions/acpx`. Manually update `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`:. \"plugins\" \"installs\" \"acpx\" \"sourcePath\"\"/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/acpx\" \" \" \"installPath\"\"/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/acpx\" \" \". ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"62704912d82649c6\">>>","score":0.6892434}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775059628904}}
