w · Discussion #36044 · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Bug: Context compaction loop runs indefinitely, burning credits with no output #36044. Bug: Context compaction loop runs indefinitely, burning credits with no output  #36044. Mar 5, 2026 · 0 comments. ## eastmotionbg Mar 5, 2026. 1. User saw \\\"compacting context\\\" status continuously 2. Documents were generated successfully (files exist on disk) but response never reached the user  Root cause Workspace files (~24KB of markdown) are injected into every message context. Combined with long conversation history and large tool outputs, the context exceeds the model window. Expected behavior  * Compaction should have a **maximum retry limit** (e.g., 3 attempts) * If compaction fails repeatedly, **notify the user** and suggest starting a new session * A **cost circuit breaker** should abort if a single turn exceeds $X without output  Actual behavior  * Compaction loops indefinitely with no retry limit * No user notification * Credits burned with no output * User had to manually notice and intervene  Reproduction  1. Have a long multi-turn session with extensive tool use (file generation, reads/writes) 3. Compacted context + workspace re-injection still exceeds limits = infinite loop  Suggested fixes  1. **Cost circuit breaker** — per-turn spending limit with user notification 3. **Lazy workspace loading** — do not re-inject full workspace files after compaction 4. **User notification** — Context too large, please start a new session  Related  * PR feat: show status reaction during context compaction #35474 adds visual feedback during compaction — good but does not fix the loop * Issues feat: show status reaction during context compaction #35422, [[Bug]: safeguard compaction makes LLM API call before checking for real messages — 48 unnecessary calls/day on idle sessions #34935](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/34935), Feature: Send user notification during context compaction #34372 mention compaction problems |. ## Replies: 0 comments. Menu       reacted with thumbs up emoji  reacted with thumbs down emoji  reacted with laugh emoji  reacted with hooray emoji  reacted with confused emoji  reacted with heart emoji  reacted with rocket emoji  reacted with eyes emoji.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a9a3a8c771af487\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.6922474\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac74dfcea8e3bb5f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenclaw and MiniMax M2.5 - Dement · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #24808 · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac74dfcea8e3bb5f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/discussions/24808\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"19c5c1fe41b5af57\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: Openclaw and MiniMax M2.5 - Dement · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #24808 · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # Openclaw and MiniMax M2.5 - Dement #24808. rmahangoe  started this conversation in General. Openclaw and MiniMax M2.5 - Dement  #24808. Feb 23, 2026 · 0 comments. ### Uh oh! There was an error while loading. ## rmahangoe Feb 23, 2026. | \\\"I have connected my OpenClaw (v2026.02.22-2) to MiniMax-M2.5 via a paid subscription. Unfortunately, the AI assistant currently lacks any persistence; it acts like a 'zombie' and fails to remember its name, soul, memory, or identity files. Furthermore, when I instruct it to perform a task such as creating a new 'Coding-Tester' agent in the workspace directory. it simply provides instructions on how I should do it rather than executing the task itself. Is this a bug in the current OpenClaw build, or is there a specific configuration fix to restore its agency and memory?\\\"  JSON  {  \\\"agentId\\\": \\\"new\\\\_agent\\\\_123\\\",  \\\"cleanup\\\": \\\"delete\\\",  \\\"table\\\": \\\"Coding-Tester\\\",  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"session\\\"  } |. Beta Was this translation helpful? You must be logged in to vote. ## Replies: 0 comments. Sign up for free **to join this conversation on GitHub**. Menu       reacted with thumbs up emoji  reacted with thumbs down emoji  reacted with laugh emoji  reacted with hooray emoji  reacted with confused emoji  reacted with heart emoji  reacted with rocket emoji  reacted with eyes emoji. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"19c5c1fe41b5af57\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.6922474\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1859029b7807a74\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nplease fix：The bug is like this: “Do not mimic this format - use proper function calling.]” when my model is Gemini 3 Pro. · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #14058 · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1859029b7807a74\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/discussions/14058\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f809637f9abd5c64\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: please fix：The bug is like this: “Do not mimic this format - use proper function calling.]” when my model is Gemini 3 Pro. · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #14058 · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab 