u signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # OpenClaw: security signal completeness across multi-account/channel paths #14118. davidahmann  started this conversation in Ideas. OpenClaw: security signal completeness across multi-account/channel paths  #14118. Feb 11, 2026 · 0 comments. ### Uh oh! There was an error while loading. ## davidahmann Feb 11, 2026. | From our current gap analysis and recent issue work, I think OpenClaw has a broader contract problem around security signal completeness in multi-account/channel environments. Core problems identified:   * Security/audit posture can drift from reality when checks or probes do not cover every configured account/path. * Probe reliability depends on canonical channel/group identifiers, but that precondition is easy to miss in real deployments. * Some high-risk behaviors are well documented but less directly exercised through account-permutation tests. Recent issue work linked to this direction:   * Security: Add --ignore-scripts to npm install during plugin installation #13132 (install supply-chain hardening tests) * [[Bug]: Telegram webhook mode allows unauthenticated update injection when webhookSecret is omitted #13116](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/13116) (webhook auth risk) * [[Bug]: [CRITICAL SECURITY] Agent Routing System Complete Failure - Communication Misdirection #13423](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/13423) (routing/security boundary concerns)   Proposal:   * Treat doctor/security output as an API contract with explicit coverage guarantees. * Add a deterministic account-permutation test matrix as a required gate for security-affecting channel changes. * Add explicit “coverage incomplete” severity when probes cannot fully execute. Question for maintainers:  Would you accept an RFC/PR slice that codifies these guarantees (coverage rules + fail-closed severity model) before adding more surface-area features? Beta Was this translation helpful? ## Replies: 0 comments. Sign up for free **to join this conversation on GitHub**. Menu       reacted with thumbs up emoji  reacted with thumbs down emoji  reacted with laugh emoji  reacted with hooray emoji  reacted with confused emoji  reacted with heart emoji  reacted with rocket emoji  reacted with eyes emoji.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"39fea4941632b7dd\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.63179934\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0e05d26177c06f0c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\ni cant install openclaw in windows 11 · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #6425 · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0e05d26177c06f0c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/discussions/6425\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2af362af2f64bf98\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: i cant install openclaw in windows 11 · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #6425 · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. halil2002sak  asked this question in Q&A. Feb 1, 2026 · 1 comment. Answered   by halil2002sak    Return to top. I'm a simple person, I don't understand much about these things 😊 Problem I used to use Linux and it worked there, but for some reason I couldn't get it to work this time, no matter what I tried? 😒) Errors ``` Error [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package ‘tslog’ imported from C:\\\\Users\\\\halil2002sak\\\\AppData\\\\Roaming\\\\npm\\\\node_modules\\\\openclaw\\\