ror [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package ‘tslog’ imported from C:\\Users\\halil2002sak\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\dist\\logging\\logger.js at Object.getPackageJSONURL (node:internal/modules/package_json_reader:316:9) at packageResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:768:81) at moduleResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:858:18) at defaultResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:990:11) at #cachedDefaultResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:718:20) at #resolveAndMaybeBlockOnLoaderThread (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:735:38) at ModuleLoader.resolveSync (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:764:52) at #resolve (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:700:17) at ModuleLoader.getOrCreateModuleJob (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:620:35) at ModuleJob.syncLink (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:143:33) { code: ‘ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND’ }  ``` |. Menu       reacted with thumbs up emoji  reacted with thumbs down emoji  reacted with laugh emoji  reacted with hooray emoji  reacted with confused emoji  reacted with heart emoji  reacted with rocket emoji  reacted with eyes emoji.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2af362af2f64bf98\">>>","score":0.6304352},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"da6a2a465907f8bc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nclawdbot: command not found · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #6594 · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"da6a2a465907f8bc\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/discussions/6594","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd0844e27a424b4d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: clawdbot: command not found · openclaw/openclaw · Discussion #6594 · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # clawdbot: command not found #6594. quorle  asked this question in Q&A. clawdbot: command not found  #6594. Feb 1, 2026 · 1 comment. ### Uh oh! There was an error while loading. ## quorle Feb 1, 2026. | I've installed a fresh installation on a newly installed Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS system. Now I can't run clawbot or issue it any commands because the command isn't found. Is there a solution for this? clawdbot: command not found  quirin@moltbot:~~$ node -v  v22.22.0  quirin@moltbot:~~$ npm -v  10.9.4  quirin@moltbot:~~$ npm prefix -g  /home/quirin/.npm-global  quirin@moltbot:~~$ echo \"$PATH\"  /home/quirin/.npm-global/bin:/home/quirin/.npm-global/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/games:/usr/local/games:/snap/bin |. ## Replies: 1 comment. ### Stxle2 Feb 1, 2026. In recent builds the CLI people used as clawdbot has shifted names (Clawdbot → Moltbot → OpenClaw), and on fresh installs the most common “command not found” cause is still npm global bin not on $PATH. ￼  Do this on Linux/macOS (bash/zsh):  **1. See what you actually have**  ``` command -v openclaw clawdbot moltbot || true; npm config get prefix; echo \"$PATH\"  ```  **2. Fix PATH (the real fix 90% of the time)**  ``` echo 'export PATH=\"$(npm config get prefix)/bin:$PATH\"' >> ~/.bashrc && . ~/.bashrc # (use ~/.zshrc if you use zsh)  ```  **3. If you want old commands back (optional compatibility)**  ``` sudo ln -sf \"$(command -v openclaw)\" /usr/local/bin/clawdbot sudo ln -sf \"$(command -v openclaw)\" /usr/local/bin/moltbot  ```  If openclaw works after step 2, it’s not a bash “bug” — it was PATH + renamed binary. Sign up for free **to join this conversation on GitHub**. Menu       reacted with thumbs up emoji  reacted with thumbs down emoji  reacted with laugh emoji  reacted with hooray emoji  reacted with confused emoji  reacted with heart emoji  reacted with rocket emoji  reacted with eyes emoji. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd0844e27a424b4d\">>>","score":0.59401023},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a74583e85b138582\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nopenclaw/openclaw · Discussions · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a74583e85b138582\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/discussions?discussions_q=is%3Aopen+sort%3Atop","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0f80fd6fb6f5b008\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n*   [Actions Automate any workflow](https://github.com/features/actions). *   [Why GitHub](https://github.com/why-github). *   [Documentation](https://docs.github.com/). *   [Marketplace](https://github.com/marketplace). [View all features](https://github.com/features). *   [Enterprises](https://github.com/enterprise). *   [Startups](https://github.com/enterprise/startups). *   [Nonprofits](https://github.com/solutions/industry/nonprofits). *   [DevSecOps](https://github.com/solutions/use-case/devsecops). *   [DevOps](https://github.com/solutions/use-case/devops). *   [Healthcare](https://github.com/solutions/industry/healthcare). *   [Manufacturing](https://github.com/solutions/industry/manufacturing). *   [Government](https://github.com/solutions/industry/government). *   [View all industries](https://github.com/solutions/industry). [View all solutions](https://github.com/solutions). *   [View all topics](https://github.com/resources/articles). *   [GitHub Skills](https://skills.github.com/). *   [Documentation](https://docs.github.com/). *   [Customer support](https://support.github.com/). *   [Partners](https://github.com/partners). [View all resources](https://github.com/resources). *   [Security Lab](https://securitylab.github.com/). *   [Maintainer Community](https://maintainers.github.com/). *   [Accelerator](https://github.com/accelerator). *   [GitHub Stars](https://stars.g